er-assisted self-interviewing) and TACASI (Telephone audio computer-assisted self-interviewing).','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.CASI','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire',13,4989,NULL,'Self-administered questionnaire: Computer-assisted (CASI)','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.CASI',452),(10745,'Capturing information in writing from a different source, or from a different medium, alphabet, or form of notation, like scientific formulae, or musical notes. For transcribed interviews or observations, it is recommended to document the primary mode of collection, using one of the interview or observation terms.','Transcription',NULL,41,5012,NULL,'Transcription','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Transcription',452),(10746,'A group discussion on a particular topic, organized for research purposes. The individuals are selected with relevance to the topic, and interaction among the participants is used as part of the method.','FocusGroup',NULL,14,4990,NULL,'Focus group','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#FocusGroup',452),(10747,'An experiment conducted in the virtual setting of the World Wide Web, in which experimental materials are programmed to implement artificial situations or events to be investigated in a distributed environment. (Reips, U.-D. (2002). Theory and techniques of Web experimenting. In B. Batinic, U.-D. Reips, & M. Bosnjak (Eds.), Online Social Sciences. Seattle: Hogrefe & Huber. Available at: http://www.websm.org/uploadi/editor/Reips_2002_Theory_and_techniques.pdf [07 June 2013])','Experiment.WebBased','Experiment',33,5009,NULL,'Web-based experiment','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Experiment.WebBased',452),(10748,'A pre-planned communication between two (or more) people - the interviewer(s) and the interviewee(s) - in which information is obtained by the interviewer(s) from the interviewee(s). If group interaction is part of the method, use \"Focus group\".','Interview',NULL,0,4976,NULL,'Interview','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Interview',452),(10749,'Observation that is conducted in a natural environment.','Observation.Field','Observation',23,4999,NULL,'Field observation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Observation.Field',452),(10750,'Computer-assisted telephone interviewing (CATI). The interviewer asks questions as directed by a computer, responses are keyed directly into the computer and the administration of the interview is managed by a specifically designed program.','Interview.Telephone.CATI','Interview.Telephone',5,4981,NULL,'Telephone interview: Computer-assisted (CATI)','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Interview.Telephone.CATI',452),(10751,'Data collection method in which the respondent reads or listens to the questions, and enters the responses by him/herself; no live interviewer is present, or participates in the questionnaire administration. If possible, use a narrower term. Use this broader term if the method is not described by any of the narrower terms - for example, for PDF and diskette questionnaires.','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire',NULL,8,4984,NULL,'Self-administered questionnaire','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire',452),(10752,'Assessment of physical properties of living beings, objects, materials, or natural phenomena. For example, findings from hands-on medical examination (e.g., palpation or auscultation), clinical measurements and lab tests like blood analysis, blood pressure, heart rate, body weight and height, as well as general measurements like time, distance, mass, temperature, force, power, speed, GPS data on physical movement and other physical parameters or variables, like geospatial data.','MeasurementsAndTests.Physical','MeasurementsAndTests',48,5019,NULL,'Physical measurements and tests','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#MeasurementsAndTests.Physical',452),(10753,'An interview conducted via the Internet. For example, interviews conducted within online forums or using web-based audio-visual technology that enables the interviewer(s) and interviewee(s) to communicate in real time.','Interview.WebBased','Interview',7,4983,NULL,'Web-based interview','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Interview.WebBased',452),(10754,'Observation that is conducted in a natural, non-controlled setting without any interaction between the researcher and his/her subjects.','Observation.Field.Nonparticipant','Observation.Field',25,5001,NULL,'Non-participant field observation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Observation.Field.Nonparticipant',452),(10755,'Statistics that relate to broad classes, groups, or categories. The data are averaged, totaled, or otherwise derived from individual-level data, and it is no longer possible to distinguish the characteristics of individuals within those classes, groups, or categories. For example, the number and age group of the unemployed in specific geographic regions, or national level statistics on the occurrence of specific offences, originally derived from the statistics of individual police districts.','Aggregation',NULL,44,5015,NULL,'Aggregation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Aggregation',452),(10756,'Narratives, stories, diaries, and written texts gathered from Internet sources, e.g. websites, blogs, discussion forums.','SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries.WebBased','SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries',21,4997,NULL,'Self-administered writings and/or diaries: Web-based','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries.WebBased',452),(10757,'Self-administered survey using a traditional paper questionnaire delivered and/or collected by mail (postal services), by fax, or in person by either interviewer, or respondent.','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.Paper','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire',10,4986,NULL,'Self-administered questionnaire: Paper','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.Paper',452),(10758,'Assessment of knowledge, skills, aptitude, or educational achievement by means of specialized measures or tests.','MeasurementsAndTests.Educational','MeasurementsAndTests',47,5018,NULL,'Educational measurements and tests','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#MeasurementsAndTests.Educational',452),(10759,'Assessment of personality traits or psychological/behavioral responses by means of specialized measures or tests. For example, objective tests like self-report measures with a restricted response format, or projective methods allowing free responses, including word association, sentence or story completion, vignettes, cartoon test, thematic apperception tests, role play, drawing tests, inkblot tests, choice ordering exercises, etc.','MeasurementsAndTests.Psychological','MeasurementsAndTests',49,5020,NULL,'Psychological measurements and tests','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#MeasurementsAndTests.Psychological',452),(10760,'Paper-and-pencil interviewing (PAPI). The interviewer uses a traditional paper questionnaire to read the questions and enter the answers.','Interview.FaceToFace.PAPI','Interview.FaceToFace',3,5022,NULL,'Face-to-face interview: Paper-and-pencil (PAPI)','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Interview.FaceToFace.PAPI',452),(10761,'Type of laboratory observation in which the researcher interacts with the subjects and often plays a role in the social situation under observation. For example, observing children\'s play in a laboratory playroom with the researcher taking part in the play.','Observation.Laboratory.Participant','Observation.Laboratory',27,5025,NULL,'Participant laboratory observation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Observation.Laboratory.Participant',452),(10762,'As a mode of secondary data collection, content coding applies coding techniques to transform qualitative data (textual, video, audio or still-image) originally produced for other purposes into quantitative data (expressed in unit-by-variable matrices) in accordance with pre-defined categorization schemes. For example, coded party manifesto data like the \"European Parliament Election Study 2009, Manifesto Study\" (doi:10.4232/1.10204).','ContentCoding',NULL,40,5011,NULL,'Content coding','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#ContentCoding',452),(10763,'Research method involving the manipulation of some or all of the independent variables included in the hypotheses.','Experiment',NULL,30,5006,NULL,'Experiment','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Experiment',452),(10764,'An experiment conducted in a natural, uncontrolled setting, in which the researcher manipulates one or several independent variables. Intervention/clinical studies are one example of field experiments.','Experiment.FieldIntervention','Experiment',32,5008,NULL,'Field/Intervention experiment','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Experiment.FieldIntervention',452),(10765,'Use if the mode of data collection is known, but not found in the list.','Other',NULL,50,5021,NULL,'Other','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Other',452),(10766,'Registering by mechanical or electronic means, in a form that allows the information to be retrieved and/or reproduced. For example, images or sounds on disc or magnetic tape.','Recording',NULL,34,5010,NULL,'Recording','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Recording',452),(10767,'Narratives, stories, diaries, and written texts created by the research subject.','SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries',NULL,18,4994,NULL,'Self-administered writings and/or diaries','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries',452),(10768,'Self-administered survey in which the respondents receive the questions incorporated in SMS (text messages) or MMS (messages including multimedia content) and send their replies in the same format.','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.SMSorMMS','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire',11,4987,NULL,'Self-administered questionnaire: Messaging (SMS/MMS)','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.SMSorMMS',452),(10769,'Presentation of information in a condensed form, by reducing it to its main points. For example, abstracts of interviews or reports that are published and used as data rather than the full-length interviews or reports.','Summary',NULL,43,5014,NULL,'Summary','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Summary',452),(10770,'Type of field observation in which the researcher interacts with the subjects and often plays a role in the social situation under observation.','Observation.Field.Participant','Observation.Field',24,5024,NULL,'Participant field observation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Observation.Field.Participant',452),(10771,'Interview administered on the telephone. Use this broader term if not CATI, or if not known whether CATI or not.','Interview.Telephone','Interview',4,4980,NULL,'Telephone interview','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Interview.Telephone',452),(10772,'An experiment conducted in a controlled, artificially created physical setting, in which a researcher manipulates one or several independent variables and measures its/their effect on the dependent variable.','Experiment.Laboratory','Experiment',31,5007,NULL,'Laboratory experiment','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Experiment.Laboratory',452),(10773,'Research method that involves collecting data as they occur (for example, observing behaviors, events, development of condition or disease, etc.), without attempting to manipulate any of the independent variables.','Observation',NULL,22,4998,NULL,'Observation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Observation',452),(10774,'Observation that is conducted in a controlled, artificially created setting. For example, observing children\'s play in a laboratory playroom.','Observation.Laboratory','Observation',26,5002,NULL,'Laboratory observation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Observation.Laboratory',452),(10775,'Computer-assisted personal interviewing (CAPI), or computer-assisted mobile interviewing (CAMI). Data collection method in which the interviewer reads questions to the respondents from the screen of a computer, laptop, or a mobile device like tablet or smartphone, and enters the answers in the same device. The administration of the interview is managed by a specifically designed program/application.','Interview.FaceToFace.CAPIorCAMI','Interview.FaceToFace',2,5023,NULL,'Face-to-face interview: Computer-assisted (CAPI/CAMI)','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Interview.FaceToFace.CAPIorCAMI',452),(10776,'Data collection method in which a live interviewer conducts a personal interview, presenting questions and entering the responses. Use this broader term if not CAPI or PAPI, or if not known whether CAPI/PAPI or not.','Interview.FaceToFace','Interview',1,4977,NULL,'Face-to-face interview','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Interview.FaceToFace',452),(10777,'The focus group participants meet in person to conduct the discussion.','FocusGroup.FaceToFace','FocusGroup',15,4991,NULL,'Face-to-face focus group','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#FocusGroup.FaceToFace',452),(10778,'Type of laboratory observation that is conducted without any interaction between the researcher and his/her subjects.','Observation.Laboratory.Nonparticipant','Observation.Laboratory',28,5004,NULL,'Non-participant laboratory observation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Observation.Laboratory.Nonparticipant',452),(10779,'Narratives, stories, diaries, and written texts submitted via e-mail messages.','SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries.Email','SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries',19,4995,NULL,'Self-administered writings and/or diaries: E-mail','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries.Email',452),(10780,'Assessing specific properties (or characteristics) of beings, things, phenomena, (and/ or processes) by applying pre-established standards and/or specialized instruments or techniques.','MeasurementsAndTests',NULL,46,5017,NULL,'Measurements and tests','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#MeasurementsAndTests',452),(10781,'Collecting and assembling data from multiple, often heterogeneous sources that have one or more reference points in common, and at least one of the sources was originally produced for other purposes. The data are incorporated in a new entity. For example, providing data on the number of universities in the last 150 years using a variety of available sources (e.g. finance documents, official statistics, university registers), combining survey data with information about geographical areas from official statistics (e.g. population density, doctors per capita, etc.), or with social media data, etc.','CompilationSynthesis',NULL,42,5013,NULL,'Compilation/Synthesis','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#CompilationSynthesis',452),(10782,'Modeling or imitative representation of real-world processes, events, or systems, often using computer programs. For example, a program modeling household consumption responses to indirect tax changes; or a dataset on hypothetical patients and their drug exposure, background conditions, and known adverse events.','Simulation',NULL,45,5016,NULL,'Simulation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Simulation',452),(10783,'Self-administered survey in which questions are presented to the respondent in the text body of an e-mail or as an attachment to an e-mail, but not as a link to a web-based questionnaire. Responses are also sent back via e-mail, in the e-mail body or as an attachment.','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.Email','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire',9,4985,NULL,'Self-administered questionnaire: E-mail','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.Email',452),(10784,'The focus group discussion is conducted over the Internet in an interactive manner.','FocusGroup.Online','FocusGroup',17,4993,NULL,'Online focus group','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#FocusGroup.Online',452),(10785,'Type of observation in which data regarding computer usage are being collected by software that can be built into the computer program itself or can be a separate program. Information may be collected about the number of users, the ways in which users interact with the program(s), how much time they spend on a page, how they use specific sections of applications, how they navigate from page to page or from one application to another, etc.','Observation.ComputerBased','Observation',29,5005,NULL,'Computer-based observation','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Observation.ComputerBased',452),(10786,'Computer-assisted web interviewing (CAWI). Data are collected using a web questionnaire, produced with a program for creating web surveys. The program can customize the flow of the questionnaire based on the answers provided, and can allow for the questionnaire to contain pictures, audio and video clips, links to different web pages etc.','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.CAWI','SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire',12,4988,NULL,'Self-administered questionnaire: Web-based (CAWI)','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredQuestionnaire.CAWI',452),(10787,'Narratives, stories, diaries, and written texts created and collected in paper form.','SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries.Paper','SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries',20,4996,NULL,'Self-administered writings and/or diaries: Paper','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#SelfAdministeredWritingsAndDiaries.Paper',452),(10788,'The focus group discussion is conducted over the telephone.','FocusGroup.Telephone','FocusGroup',16,4992,NULL,'Telephone focus group','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#FocusGroup.Telephone',452),(10789,'Collecting information on objects or phenomena without physical contact with them, using remote sensors on satellites and aircraft (planes, drones, weather balloons). Often used to gather information on the Earth’s surface, atmosphere and oceans. For example, damage assessment after an earthquake or forest fires. The technique is also used for military, commercial, economic and other applications.','Recording.RemoteSensing','Recording',35,NULL,NULL,'Recording: Remote sensing','https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_4.0.html#Recording.RemoteSensing',452),(10809,'','SND',NULL,16,10491,NULL,'Swedish National Data Service (SND)','https://vocabularies.cessda.eu/vocabulary/CdcPublisherNames_SND?v=2.0',454),(10810,'','CSDA',NULL,1,10478,NULL,'Czech Social Science Data Archive (ČSDA)','https://vocabularies.cessda.eu/vocabulary/CdcPublisherNames_CSDA?v=2.0',454),(10811,''